  "schema": "orcel-donor-provenance/1",
  "packet": "WP1-01",
  "note": "Machine-readable index of every vendored, copied or adapted donor file under crates/, apps/, packages/ and tests/ (and a few outside them). Each donor names its source repository, its pin (a 40-hex commit, or a registry release with its SHA-256), the upstream licence, the notice in the repository, the founder attestation that records permission (kept separate from the upstream licence terms, founder decision 2026-11-17) and the detailed per-task provenance records it consolidates. A path ending in '/' covers the whole directory and names its patch queue (\"patches\": a file, or \"none\"). Each donor's licence_text (else its notice) must carry the text of its declared licence. This central manifest stands in for per-directory PROVENANCE.json files: each entry carries the same fields {repo, sha, paths, licence, attestation_ref, patches}, and one file lets the gate cross-check allowlists, records and attestations in one place. 'references' lists files that name a donor notice or hold a provenance record without being donor code. Checked by scripts/check-donor-provenance.mjs.",
